\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The present model against the closest related model families. FvCB: Farquhar--von Caemmerer--Berry biochemistry. ``Carbon input'' distinguishes models that compute assimilation from gas exchange at every step (\emph  {comp.}) from those that prescribe it through a light-use-efficiency term, a radiation-use coefficient or a look-up table (\emph  {presc.}). ``Fast--slow'' marks an explicit numerical separation of the algebraic gas-exchange subsystem from the differential growth subsystem. ``Num.\ verif.'' marks published convergence, conservation or estimator-verification evidence, as distinct from agreement with data. Entries describe the standard formulations as given in the cited references; individual modules and versions differ.}}{5}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:related}{{1}{5}{The present model against the closest related model families. FvCB: Farquhar--von Caemmerer--Berry biochemistry. ``Carbon input'' distinguishes models that compute assimilation from gas exchange at every step (\emph {comp.}) from those that prescribe it through a light-use-efficiency term, a radiation-use coefficient or a look-up table (\emph {presc.}). ``Fast--slow'' marks an explicit numerical separation of the algebraic gas-exchange subsystem from the differential growth subsystem. ``Num.\ verif.'' marks published convergence, conservation or estimator-verification evidence, as distinct from agreement with data. Entries describe the standard formulations as given in the cited references; individual modules and versions differ}{table.1}{}}
