\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Diel starch and sucrose dynamics for the 4, 6, 8, 12 and 18\nobreakspace  {}h photoperiods. Simulated traces are compared with the measured diel profiles of the repository reference file (see Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:protocol}). Each panel prints the nRMSE and the fitted multiplicative scale. The scale is between $0.86$ and $1.15$ for starch at the four fitted photoperiods and between $2.25$ and $3.31$ for sucrose, so the sucrose comparison is one of shape and timing and not of absolute level. The 18\nobreakspace  {}h column was not used in any fit; its starch nRMSE is not reported, because the fitted scale of $0.07$ absorbs the divergence described in Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:results:envelope}.}}{24}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:carb}{{4}{24}{Diel starch and sucrose dynamics for the 4, 6, 8, 12 and 18~h photoperiods. Simulated traces are compared with the measured diel profiles of the repository reference file (see Section~\ref {sec:protocol}). Each panel prints the nRMSE and the fitted multiplicative scale. The scale is between $0.86$ and $1.15$ for starch at the four fitted photoperiods and between $2.25$ and $3.31$ for sucrose, so the sucrose comparison is one of shape and timing and not of absolute level. The 18~h column was not used in any fit; its starch nRMSE is not reported, because the fitted scale of $0.07$ absorbs the divergence described in Section~\ref {sec:results:envelope}}{figure.4}{}}
